52,279,98,1,453,449,200,116,131,475,500,346,281,462]"],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["[499,438,364,210,178,126]"],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["[4,1,5,4,1,1,4,2,3,4,3,2,2,5,1,4,3,4,3,5,4,4,1,3]"],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["[3,2,2,2,5,2,5,2]"],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["[4,3,2,5,2,3,2,4]"],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["[63,1,390,390,93,186]"],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["[1,1,3,3,4,5]"],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["[212,211,211,211,209,209]"],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["[402,346,404,21,409,83]"],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["[3,4,5,4,3,4]"],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["[1,260]"],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["[6,5,2,2,2,2,5,5]"],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["[365,304]"],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["[168,1,1,1,1,193,500,1,500,78,500,333,416,125,500,338,494,344,297,500]"],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["[1,3,5,3,3,3,5,5,1,4,5,5,2,5,5,3,1,4]"],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["[1,2,1,2,2,2,1,1,2,2,2,1,2,1,1,1,2,2,1,2]"],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["[125,18,18,18,124,18,18,124,18,18,124,18]"],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["[128,128,115,115,115,128,128,128,128,115,128,115,115,128,128,115,115,128,115,128,115,115,128,128]"],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["[5,5,5,4,4,3,2,1,1,1]"],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["[116,113,110,108,108,108,108,108]"],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["[5,5,2,4,1,1,2,3,2,3,5,1,2,1,1,2,3,5,1,5,2,5]"],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["[464,263]"],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":[],"out":"\"#4:5b5c98ef514dbfa5\"","perf":{"label":"500 piles","gen":"int[] a0 = BCB.ints(500, 1, 499); int sum = 0; for (int x : a0) sum += x; if (sum % 2 == 0) a0[0]++;","floorMs":2000},"refMs":3}],"lesson":"dp-trees-intervals","statement":"An even number of piles of stones is arranged in a row; pile `i` has `piles[i]` stones, and the total number of stones is **odd**, so there are no ties.\n\nAlice and Bob take turns, Alice first. On each turn a player takes the entire pile from **either end** of the row. When no piles remain, the player with more stones wins. Assuming both play optimally, return `true` if Alice wins and `false` if Bob wins.","constraints":["2 <= piles.length <= 500","`piles.length` is even","1 <= piles[i] <= 500","`sum(piles)` is odd"],"hints":["Interval DP: let dp[i][j] be the best (current player − other player) difference on piles i..j.","dp[i][j] = max(piles[i] − dp[i + 1][j], piles[j] − dp[i][j − 1]). Alice wins when dp[0][n − 1] > 0.","There is also a one-line answer. Colour the piles by even and odd index: Alice can always take all piles of one colour, and one colour has more stones because the total is odd."],"explain":"Alice takes the 5 at the start. Whatever end Bob takes from [3,4,5], Alice can take a 5 or 4 next and finish with 9 or 10 stones out of 17, so the answer is `true`."},
